# Real athlete screening PDFs — NEVER commit. Local calibration/verification
# samples for the HoloMotion ingest pipeline live here.
backend/scripts/samples/
*.pdf
!reports/FYP-I-Report.pdf

# The ONE screening-shaped PDF that is safe to commit, and the exception is
# deliberately a single exact path rather than a directory: the blanket *.pdf
# rule above exists to stop a real athlete's report being committed by accident,
# and a `!backend/scripts/fixtures/` would re-open that door for anything dropped
# in there later.
#
# It is generated by `npm run make:fixture` from fabricated values and a
# fabricated name, contains no athlete, and is UNCOMPRESSED so a diff is
# readable. It exists because the checks that verify the extraction pipeline and
# the name-redaction boundary previously needed the real reports, which means
# they could not run in CI or on a fresh clone at all.
!backend/scripts/fixtures/synthetic-report.pdf

# Tesseract OCR language-model cache (name-redaction pass)
backend/.tesseract/

# TypeScript incremental build info
*.tsbuildinfo

# Claude Code session state
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/projects/
.claude/wakeup_jobs/

# Local-only tooling
sync-to-submission.ps1
SUBMISSION_WORKFLOW.md

# Added by `vercel link`. `.vercel/` holds the project id; `.env*` covers the
# .env.local the CLI writes (it carries a short-lived OIDC token).
#
# The negation is not decoration: `.env*` also matches backend/.env.example and
# frontend/.env.local.example, which are COMMITTED templates. Tracked files stay
# tracked, so nothing broke today — but the day someone re-adds one it would be
# silently ignored, and a missing example file is exactly the kind of absence
# nobody notices.
.vercel
.env*
!*.example

# Rendered deliverable — regenerate with backend/scripts/guide-to-pdf.js
AIRMS-System-Guide.pdf
